  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat (filed by an agent), 2026-11-12: \"Bug, we should be able to pick different machine and different post processor - on each setup. It should be considered P1-P3\".\n\n**What happens.** In the app the maintainer finds no working way to give one setup its own machine and its own post processor while another setup keeps a different pair.\n\n**What exists underneath.** The capability shipped with #343 and #388 (both closed): `crates/app/src/setup_mount.rs` - a setup either owns its mount (`SetupDef::machine` / `SetupDef::post`) or follows the document's; generation, the spindle law, limits and posting read each operation's own setup, and a program with several mounts posts one file per mount. The commands are in `crates/app/src/commands/setup_mount.rs`, the MCP tools in `crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs`, the UI side in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/machines_pane.rs` and `crates/ui/src/state_setup_mount.rs`. So this is a defect in what the UI offers or does, not a missing model. Things that changed around it recently and may have hidden or broken the path: the Setups page declutter (#1104 / PR #1114), the machine-mode ribbon door (#1195 / PR #1200), the Machine page.\n\n**Rated P3** (wrong behaviour with a workaround: the MCP tools can set a setup's mount). If reproducing shows worse - e.g. a setup posts through another setup's post, or is generated against another setup's machine - re-rate it P1 and say so here.\n\n**To do first.** Reproduce in a UI test with two setups: say exactly which step is missing or wrong (no control on the Setup<n> page? the control changes the document's mount instead of the setup's? the pick is shown but not stored? the post picker is missing while the machine picker works?) and comment that on this issue before fixing.\n\nDone means: from each setup's own page the user can pick that setup's machine and that setup's post processor (and set it back to \"follow the document\"); the pick is an undoable command on that setup only; the page shows which machine and post each setup uses; pinned by a UI test with two setups on different machines and posts whose posted output is one file per mount, each through its own post. Nothing was checked on screen by the filing agent.\n",
